6130: # A ledger entry's bridge_outcome that counts as a usable reply: EXACTLY 'usable reply' or (wave
6131: # 24) 'usable reply (after a timeout continuation)' - the reply of the ONE continuation turn the
6132: # bridge ran on the thread of a turn it had killed on its timeout. (wave 24b, F13-2) Any other
6133: # string - a future 'usable reply (<something>)' too - is not usable until it is added here: the
6134: # predicate clears the endpoint health, evidences a sign-in (RecentUsable) and counts on the
6135: # scoreboard, so it fails closed.
6136: $script:UsableOutcomes = @('usable reply', 'usable reply (after a timeout continuation)')
6137: function Test-UsableOutcome {
6138:     param([string]$Outcome)
6139:     return [bool]($script:UsableOutcomes -ccontains $Outcome)
6140: }
